<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Italo-Ethiopian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1935">1935</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Italy's 1935 invasion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Italo-Ethiopian War was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a>'s invasion and conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1935–1936. Italian forces used aircraft and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poison-gas">poison gas</a>, and Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> went into exile. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> imposed ineffective <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>, and the conquest became a centrepiece of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> and a defining crisis for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-italo-ethiopian-war.jpg" alt="Second Italo-Ethiopian War" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Passo_Uarieu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
